{"kind":"report","text":"Planner disposition for d182bca0 (A2 package boundary and result API), after reading notes/implementation/2026-10-18-archive-a2-preparation.md at 5d6d53c0 first and in full, section 15.7, and checker consultations 85143d73, f2b69d75 and 004ada62.\n\nDecided: keep the public SDK portable; add a source-only Node composition for clone replay. Take the proposed boundary as written in the note's two tables, with these fixed points.\n\n1. Ownership. packages/git/src/journal-reader.ts and journal-local.ts own archive object and tree validation, bounded local object reads and ref resolution, reusing the A1 explicit-format parsers for both object formats; Git imports no replay code. packages/replay/src/archive.ts owns ArchiveReadPort, archiveSource and verifyArchive and imports neither Git nor Node, including through types, dynamic imports, re-exports or relative paths. packages/replay/src/git.ts composes gitSource(directory) from the two; bin.ts injects the Node and file ports. No duplicated parser.\n\n2. Publication. Git becomes a development dependency of replay's source manifest only. The published manifest keeps its runtime dependencies (contract, bytes, derive) and the same six-package membership; Git is not an unpublished runtime dependency. The release plan excludes exactly git.ts and bin.ts as Node-only production inputs and the ./git source export, by name, with the output-closure check extended so neither reaches staged JS or declarations; keep negative witnesses for a leaked Node or Git import or output and for an unlisted exemption. Any further Node-only helper needs its own named exclusion; no directory-wide exception. Clone replay does not ship in the public SDK in this milestone; publishing it would be a separate decision, which I am not taking now.\n\n3. Guard. The active-source exception names only git.ts, its bounded tests and the replay manifest's development dependency. The guard keeps refusing Git-to-Replay dependencies and portable Replay-to-Git reaches. Fixtures may use Git explicitly and confer no runtime authority.\n\n4. Results. verifyArchive checks archive structure first, then calls the unchanged native verifier and judges. Its result keeps a typed archive failure distinct from a completed native Verification: structural corruption (a changed line, a cut segment, an inconsistent head.json, a ref that names no commit, a tree without head.json) is mismatch at its actual read location, with no invented native target, hash, coverage or report; unsafe forms (symlink, submodule, executable, out-of-grammar path) are refused without touching the filesystem; unavailable reads, deadlines and work limits keep their own meanings and are never recast as mismatch; a genuinely absent foreign ref is missing-dependency; a valid staged-ref snapshot reaches native replay and stays incomplete for unwalked ancestry, never missing-input. On success the real native report, coverage and why are retained; nothing upgrades native consistency or coverage. A source-selected head lists archive-head under trusts even when passed internally as the expected head; a caller's --head or --receipt stays a separate pin. Receipt prefix membership is checked only after integrity and continuity succeed through the resolved archive head, then on the receipt's own scope, incarnation, position and hash; a receipt past a valid head is behind; a matching earlier receipt never bypasses a later corrupt entry. --texts and --receipt use separate bounded caller-selected file ports that archive tree paths cannot reach.\n\n5. Section 15.7 reconciliation. The note's \"artroom-replay gains a second source\" is met by the repository's replay command; the published portable package does not gain it. Carry a one-sentence amendment to section 15.7 saying so in the A2 head (document-only, same review), rather than leaving the design and the release plan in disagreement.\n\nOut of scope, unchanged: real-history export, admission, consent and disclosures, A4, A5, progress, G1 and any provider deployment. The dependent A2 source may proceed under f27603e7; gate once at the submitted head before exact-head checker review.","body":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d182bca0dece98711f5213d26456287f4de79ed5","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}